/* ============================================================================
   AltText Line Chart UDFs and Required Measures
   Repository: https://github.com/Juls-BI/powerbi-alttext-udfs
   Author: Juliana Smith
   Purpose:
   This file contains reusable DAX UDFs and supporting measures for generating
   accessible, descriptive alt text for line charts in Power BI.

   Contents:
   - AltText_LineChart UDF
   - Required base measures list
   - Example final measure for calling the UDF

   Notes:
   - All UDFs in this repository follow the same documentation pattern.
   - Measures listed here must exist in the data model for the UDF to work.
   - This file is safe to copy into any Power BI model.
   ============================================================================
*/

/* ============================================================================
   AltText_LineChart UDF
   Purpose:
   Generates dynamic, descriptive alt text for line charts showing Revenue and Cost trends.
   Includes month over month (MoM) and year to date (YTD) insights, with contextual wording
   based on percentage changes and current vs previous month values.

   Key Features:
   - Automatically detects trend strength (strong, slight, stable)
   - Provides formatted numeric and percentage comparisons
   - Summarises YTD totals for Revenue and Cost
   - Designed for accessibility and executive level clarity

   Inputs:
   TrendPeriod, MeasuresText, CategoryText, FiltersText, UnitsText

   Outputs:
   Structured alt text combining trend, measure, filter, and insight clauses
   ============================================================================
*/

DEFINE

FUNCTION AltText_LineChart =
(
    TrendPeriod: STRING,
    MeasuresText: STRING,
    CategoryText: STRING,
    FiltersText: STRING,
    UnitsText: STRING
) =>

/* --- GLOBAL MoM logic --- */
VAR RevChange = [MoM % Revenue (Global)]
VAR CostChange = [MoM % Cost (Global)]

VAR CurrentMonth = [Latest Reporting Month]
VAR PrevMonth    = [Previous Reporting Month]

/* --- Current and Previous Month Values --- */
VAR RevCurrent = [Revenue Current (Global)]
VAR RevPrev    = [Revenue Previous (Global)]

VAR CostCurrent = [Cost Current (Global)]
VAR CostPrev    = [Cost Previous (Global)]

/* --- YTD Values --- */
VAR RevYTD  = [Revenue YTD (Global)]
VAR CostYTD = [Cost YTD (Global)]

/* --- Trend wording --- */
VAR RevTrendText =
    SWITCH(
        TRUE(),
        ISBLANK(RevChange), "Revenue trend unavailable",
        RevChange > 0.05,  "Revenue is increasing strongly",
        RevChange > 0,     "Revenue is increasing slightly",
        RevChange < -0.05, "Revenue is decreasing significantly",
        RevChange < 0,     "Revenue is decreasing slightly",
        "Revenue is stable"
    )

VAR CostTrendText =
    SWITCH(
        TRUE(),
        ISBLANK(CostChange), "Cost trend unavailable",
        CostChange > 0.05,  "Cost is increasing strongly",
        CostChange > 0,     "Cost is increasing slightly",
        CostChange < -0.05, "Cost is decreasing significantly",
        CostChange < 0,     "Cost is decreasing slightly",
        "Cost is stable"
    )

/* --- Detailed insight sentences --- */
VAR CostInsight =
    CostTrendText & ". Current month cost is " &
    FORMAT(CostCurrent, "#,##0") & ", " &
    FORMAT(CostChange, "0.0%") & " " &
    IF(CostChange < 0, "lower", "higher") &
    " than the previous month (" &
    FORMAT(CostPrev, "#,##0") & "). "

VAR RevInsight =
    RevTrendText & ". Current month revenue is " &
    FORMAT(RevCurrent, "#,##0") & ", " &
    FORMAT(RevChange, "0.0%") & " " &
    IF(RevChange < 0, "lower", "higher") &
    " than the previous month (" &
    FORMAT(RevPrev, "#,##0") & "). "

/* --- YTD sentence --- */
VAR YTDInsight =
    "Year to date revenue is " & FORMAT(RevYTD, "#,##0") &
    " and year to date cost is " & FORMAT(CostYTD, "#,##0") & ". "

/* --- Clauses in your preferred order --- */
VAR TrendClause =
    IF ( ISBLANK ( TrendPeriod ), "", "Trend over " & TrendPeriod & ". " )

VAR MeasuresClause =
    IF ( ISBLANK ( MeasuresText ), "", "Measures shown: " & MeasuresText & ". " )

VAR CategoryClause =
    IF ( ISBLANK ( CategoryText ), "", "Categories: " & CategoryText & ". " )

VAR FiltersClause =
    IF ( ISBLANK ( FiltersText ), "", "Filters applied: " & FiltersText & ". " )

VAR UnitsClause =
    IF ( ISBLANK ( UnitsText ), "", "Units: " & UnitsText & ". " )

RETURN
    TrendClause &
    MeasuresClause &
    CategoryClause &
    FiltersClause &
    CostInsight &
    RevInsight &
    YTDInsight &
    UnitsClause


/* ============================================================================
   REQUIRED MEASURES FOR AltText_LineChart
   These measures MUST exist in the data model for the UDF to work correctly.
   All must return numeric or date values as specified.

   IMPORTANT:
   If your model uses different measure names than the ones listed below,
   you MUST update the UDF to reference your actual measure names.
   The UDF does NOT auto-detect or adapt to renamed measures.

   1. MoM % Measures (numeric)
      - [MoM % Revenue (Global)]
      - [MoM % Cost (Global)]
      Purpose: Used for trend detection and MoM comparisons.

   2. Reporting Month Measures (date)
      - [Latest Reporting Month]
      - [Previous Reporting Month]
      Purpose: Identifies current and previous periods.

   3. Current Month Values (numeric)
      - [Revenue Current (Global)]
      - [Cost Current (Global)]
      Purpose: Used in narrative sentences for current month values.

   4. Previous Month Values (numeric)
      - [Revenue Previous (Global)]
      - [Cost Previous (Global)]
      Purpose: Used in narrative sentences for previous month values.

   5. YTD Values (numeric)
      - [Revenue YTD (Global)]
      - [Cost YTD (Global)]
      Purpose: Used for year-to-date summary sentence.

   6. Text Inputs (text)
      - [Trend Period]
      - [Region Filters]
      Purpose: Passed directly into the UDF as descriptive text.

   Notes:
   - All numeric measures must return numbers, not formatted text.
   - All date measures must return valid date values.
   - Text measures must return plain text without formatting.
   - If you rename any measure in your model, update the UDF accordingly.
   ============================================================================
*/

   EXAMPLE: Final Measure Calling the UDF
   This measure shows how to call the AltText_LineChart UDF from your model.

   Notes:
   - Replace [Trend Period] and [Region Filters] with your own text measures.
   - UnitsText ("GBP") can be changed to any currency or unit.
   - CategoryText is optional and can be replaced with a category list measure.
   ============================================================================
*/

AltText_LineChart_Final =
AltText_LineChart(
    [Trend Period],          -- TrendPeriod (text)
    "Revenue and Cost",      -- MeasuresText (text)
    BLANK(),                 -- CategoryText (text or blank)
    [Region Filters],        -- FiltersText (text)
    "GBP"                    -- UnitsText (text)
)
